)
```

So it places at the center of a single tile. If I use the building's bottom-right tile (workplace.x + 1, workplace.y + 1), the citizen will appear near the center of the farm (bottom-right of the 2x2 grid). That seems reasonable.

But wait, I should also think about what happens when the citizen leaves work. The return path goes from the citizen's position to the house. If the citizen is inside the building footprint, the current position won't be on a road, and `shortestRoadPathToHouse` requires the start to be on a road:

```typescript
